 "answer": "The feature is **iterative index scans**, available starting with pgvector 0.8.0. The README says: \"Starting with 0.8.0, you can enable iterative index scans, which will automatically scan more of the index until enough results are found (or it reaches `hnsw.max_scan_tuples` or `ivfflat.max_probes`).\" [pgvector/README.md]\n\nYou enable it per session for HNSW indexes with:\n\n\"SET hnsw.iterative_scan = strict_order;\" [pgvector/README.md]\n\nUse `relaxed_order` instead for better recall, at the cost of results that may be slightly out of distance order. For IVFFlat, the setting is `ivfflat.iterative_scan`. [pgvector/README.md]",
